## Current Pipeline Analysis

```
[tgz file]
    │
    ▼
extract to /tmp          ← Stage 1: I/O write  (100K files × decompress)
    │
    ▼
encrypt each file        ← Stage 2: CPU + I/O read+write (100K files)
→ save to /tmp/enc/
    │
    ▼
aws s3 sync /tmp/enc/    ← Stage 3: Network (100K small PUT requests)
    │
    ▼
cleanup /tmp             ← Stage 4: I/O (rm 200K files)
```

### Bottleneck Map

| Stage | Bottleneck | Cost per tgz |
|---|---|---|
| Extract | Disk write 100K files | High inode/metadata overhead |
| Encrypt each file | CPU + 2× disk R/W per file | **Worst: 200K file ops** |
| s3 sync | 100K PUT requests, TLS per file | **Worst: latency × 100K** |
| Cleanup | `rm` on 100K files | Surprisingly slow |

**You are doing ~400K file-level operations per tgz × 5000 tgz = 2 billion file ops total.**

