## Optimized Pipeline: Stream Everything, Touch Disk Minimally

```
[tgz file]
    │
    ▼ (never extract to disk)
tar -xzf | per-file encrypt | re-tar | aws s3 cp stream
    │
    ▼
/yyyy/MM/dd/filename.tar.enc  (one object per tgz, or sharded)
```

### Core Insight

```
BEFORE:  tgz → 100K files on disk → 100K encrypted files on disk → 100K S3 PUTs
AFTER:   tgz → pipe → encrypt stream → pipe → 1 S3 PUT (multipart)
```

You already proved **1 big stream = 100MB/s**. Keep it that way end-to-end.

