## Recommended Final Architecture

```
12 parallel pipelines (one per vCPU):

tgz_file
  │
  zcat ──────────────────────────────────── ~500 MB/s decompress
  │
  openssl enc -aes-256-ctr (AES-NI) ─────── ~3 GB/s encrypt  
  │
  aws s3 cp - s3://bucket/yyyy/MM/dd/x.enc ─ ~100 MB/s upload
  │
  (no /tmp, no cleanup needed)

Total throughput target: 12 workers × 90MB/s = ~1 GB/s
5000 tgz × 10GB avg = 50TB / 1GB/s = ~14 hours
```

The elimination of 400K file operations per tgz is the single biggest win — everything else is tuning around that.
